  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already caches its only external dependency (the Windhawk installer) with actions/cache/restore and actions/cache/save using a version-scoped key, which satisfies the P-LIT-GHA-CACHE dependency-caching intent; there is no separate pip/npm install step whose dependencies would benefit from an additional cache. P-LIT-FAIL-FAST is contraindicated because this is a cross-version mod compatibility check in which every matrix outcome is required, so canceling remaining cells after a failure would reduce intended build/test coverage. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT is not supported: the CI history is explicitly not a measured baseline, jobs complete in minutes, and no safe timeout bound is established, so imposing one risks failing valid slow or cold-cache runs. The remaining patterns (Bazel parallelism/incremental/deps, test selection/prioritization, environment snapshots, schedule suppression, unused outputs) do not fit this mod-compilation workflow or would alter coverage. No supported optimization preserves the intended coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT"]
}
